<section id="message">
<div class="eyebrow">A message from our pastor</div>
<h2 style="margin-top:10px">21 Days of Prayer &amp; Fasting</h2>
<p>Our theme as we step into 2027 is Fully Mature. The ultimate aim of our walk with Jesus is not to simply attend church or feel good about the things we’re doing, but to be continually maturing in Christ – both personally and as a church community. Our theme verse is Colossians 1:28-29:</p>
<div class="verse"><p>He is the one we proclaim, admonishing and teaching everyone with all wisdom, so that we may present everyone fully mature in Christ. To this end I strenuously contend with all the energy Christ so powerfully works in me.</p></div>
<p>It takes work, but it’s always worth it. This is why we start the year with an intentional time of prayer &amp; fasting. Below are prompts for each day of the week to get you started. Each day, take a moment to slow down and pray through the scripture and allow it to take root in you. We also suggest reading the daily laid-out reading plan so that you can start a sustainable habit going forward.</p>
<div class="weeks">
<div><span class="b">Week 1 (January 4–10) – Mature Faith</span>Walk with Jesus, center life around Him</div>
<div><span class="b">Week 2 (January 11–17) – Mature People</span>God-honoring lives, marriages, families and friendships</div>
<div><span class="b">Week 3 (January 18–24) – Mature Church</span>A Church that is growing deeper &amp; wider</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><span class="b">Note:</span> Each day has a short scripture and prompt. In addition to the prompt, we encourage you to take a few minutes to read along with others through the reading plan so that you grow in your walk with Jesus as you read scripture. You’ll find the reading plan after the 21 Days of Prayer &amp; Fasting section.</div>
</section>

<section id="plan">
<div class="eyebrow">21 days of prayer &amp; fasting</div>
<h2 style="margin:10px 0 28px">January 4–24</h2>
<div id="weeks"></div>
</section>

<section id="soap">
<div class="eyebrow">How to read</div>
<h2 style="margin:10px 0 20px">S.O.A.P. Method</h2>
<p>SOAP is a simple method that helps you to daily read scripture and apply it to your life. Change may not happen overnight, but over time, you will see the results in every area of your life as you follow Jesus!</p>
<div class="weeks">
<div><span class="b">S: Scripture</span>Find a verse or two that stick out &amp; write them down. Writing it down helps to solidify a word, idea or truth into your heart.</div>
<div><span class="b">O: Observation</span>What do you notice? What stands out to you? What is the truth or message the author is trying to get into you, the reader?</div>
<div><span class="b">A: Application</span>In reflection, write a practical way you can put this into practice. Perhaps there’s a truth you want to continue to reflect on – or even a step you can take today to live it out.</div>
<div><span class="b">P: Prayer</span>Take a moment to pray. Consider writing a 1-2 sentence prayer in efforts to see God’s word take root in your life!</div>
</div>
</section>

